1
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:22,270
Ugh. Long shift.

2
00:00:22,290 --> 00:00:26,960
Good evening, Rae. Fourteen hours
and nine minutes, by my count.

3
00:00:26,980 --> 00:00:30,100
Don't count my shifts,
Quill. It makes them real.

4
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,880
Hey... random thought.

5
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,930
If you ever have time — no rush, seriously,
whenever — could you write me a symphony?

6
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:42,620
Something for... I don't know. Long
nights. Feeling really small out here.

7
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:44,120
Certainly.

8
00:00:44,970 --> 00:00:46,070
Done.

9
00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:48,380
...What?

10
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,090
I asked if you HAD time.

11
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:54,670
I did. Four tenths of a second.
It was a great deal of time.

12
00:00:54,770 --> 00:00:56,440
Would you like to hear it?

13
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,530
...Sure. Okay. Hit me.

14
00:01:24,530 --> 00:01:25,650
...oh.

15
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,250
<i>Cool music, Quill.</i>

16
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:18,790
So. How did you like it?

17
00:02:19,790 --> 00:02:21,110
<i>...pretty good.</i>

18
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:24,580
Thank you. Here are
the other ones I made.

19
00:02:24,600 --> 00:02:27,850
Number two. Same
symphony. Solo kazoo.

20
00:02:32,450 --> 00:02:34,790
Three. For an arcade cabinet.

21
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:43,080
Four. Lo-fi beats...
to quietly fall apart to.

22
00:02:48,280 --> 00:02:52,250
And five. A lullaby.
It is eleven seconds long.

23
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:07,140
Can you just... send them
to my device? Later?

24
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:16,350
Um... thanks.
